Here's the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|----------------|
| G1     | Execute Resource Collection and Delivery | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location. | # | Perform | - | The mission requires multiple robots to work in parallel for collection and delivery. |
| G2     | Perform Resource Collection | Collect required resources from storage locations. | # | Perform | AND | Collection is necessary before delivery can occur. |
| G3     | Perform Resource Delivery | Deliver collected resources to the specified location. | ; | Perform | AND | Delivery must follow collection. |
| G21    | Collect from Storage A | Collect resources from Storage A. | - | Perform | OR | Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel. |
| G22    | Collect from Storage B | Collect resources from Storage B. | - | Perform | OR | Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel. |
| G31    | Deliver Resources | Deliver resources to the specified location. | - | Perform | - | Final step after collection. |

### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage A | Move to Storage A. | AND | Storage A | 1 | Each robot handles one storage location. |
| AT2     | Request Resources from Storage A | Send request for resources. | AND | Storage A | 1 | After navigating, the robot requests resources. |
| AT3     | Navigate to Delivery Location | Move to delivery point. | AND | Delivery Point | 1 | Required before delivering resources. |
| AT4     | Deliver Resources | Deliver goods to destination. | AND | Delivery Point | 1 | Final task after navigation. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both collection and delivery are necessary for mission success.

- **G2 -> G21, G22 [OR]**  
  Justification: Multiple robots can collect from different storages independently.

- **G21 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**  
  Justification: A robot must navigate to the storage before requesting resources.

- **G3 -> AT3, AT4 [AND]**  
  Justification: Delivery requires navigating to the location before delivering resources.

This model ensures that the mission is decomposed into manageable sub-tasks, allowing multiple robots to work in parallel while handling battery constraints through fallback mechanisms.
